---
/** Option controls for changing a GIF's speed or playing it backwards, shared by the tool page and its landing pages. */
interface Props { defaults?: Record<string, string> }
const { defaults = {} } = Astro.props;
import OptionDetails from '../OptionDetails.astro';
const speed = defaults.speed ?? '2';
const speeds = [
  ['0.25', '0.25× (4 times slower)'],
  ['0.5', '0.5× (half speed)'],
  ['0.75', '0.75×'],
  ['1', '1× (same speed)'],
  ['1.5', '1.5×'],
  ['2', '2× (twice as fast)'],
  ['3', '3×'],
  ['4', '4× (four times as fast)'],
] as const;
---
<div class="field">
  <label for="speed">Speed</label>
  <select id="speed">
    {speeds.map(([v, l]) => <option value={v} selected={v === speed}>{l}</option>)}
  </select>
</div>
<div class="field">
  <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="reverse" checked={defaults.reverse === 'true'} /> Play it backwards</label>
</div>
<OptionDetails>
  <p>Every frame’s time is multiplied by the speed and rounded to a hundredth of a second. Browsers show anything under 0.02 s as about 0.1 s, so a GIF that is already very fast cannot be made faster: its frames stop at 0.02 s.</p>
  <p>Backwards plays the frames last to first, each with its own time, and the loop setting is kept.</p>
</OptionDetails>
